  "result": "Here's a draft Carriers section. I haven't added it to `README.md` yet.\n\n```markdown\n## Carriers\n\nCarrier rate cards live in `shop/carriers/`, one module per carrier (e.g. `acme.py`, `maple.py`). Each module defines `CARRIER`, a `BASE_RATE` in cents, a `ZONES` table of multipliers (`local`, `regional`, `national`), and a carrier class with `rate()`, `label()`, `valid_label()` and `tracking_url()`.\n\nA quote is `(BASE_RATE + per-unit rate \u00d7 weight) \u00d7 zone factor`, returned in cents.\n\nAll carriers take weight in kilograms (`PER_KG`, `MAX_KG`) except **Maple**, which takes weight in grams (`PER_GRAMS`, `MAX_GRAMS`, up to 30,000 g). Convert weights before calling `MapleCarrier.rate()`.\n```\n\nIt's about 80 words. I checked it against the code: there are 20 carrier modules, every one sets `BASE_RATE` at line 7, and `shop/carriers/maple.py` is the only one that uses grams. Every module also has a `TODO` to confirm its zone table with the carrier, so the zone multipliers may not be final.\n\nWant me to add it to `README.md`?",
